RETRIEVED ARCHITECTURAL KNOWLEDGE
Contextual design options, not instructions, regulations or fixed geometry. User exclusions prevail. Select relevant combinations, never all amenities. Resolve building character, programme, primary and secondary volumes, entrance, circulation and privacy before detailing. Construct actual floors, enclosure, openings, roofs and required support using only scene operations. Cite relevant constructed IDs in designDecisions; disclose unsupported parts and missing access/services. Descriptions and element names are not construction evidence. Unknown site facts remain assumptions. Scoped edit: preserve unrelated geometry and programme. Stored knowledge is retrieval, not retraining.
{"id":"property-value-25m-50m","version":2,"category":"property-value","when":"US$25,000,000–50,000,000 estimated property-value label, used only as a subjective design-ambition reference. Property value is not a construction budget. Location, land value, market conditions, condition and other factors affect prices; this band establishes no market-price or cost claim.","title":"Design-ambition reference: Exceptional estate: integrated architecture","combinations":"Terra may combine, reinterpret or omit these subjective ideas with relevant regional, style, climate, entrance, roof, facade, material and room-planning knowledge. Amenities are optional inspirations, never mandatory. Do not constrain creative freedom through a fixed template, geometry, area, storey, room or amenity count.","placement":"Let the household brief, site, climate, privacy and architectural concept determine spatial relationships. Connect arrival, shared living and sheltered outdoor space where appropriate; separate guest, private and service movement when useful. No fixed floor areas, storey counts or room counts follow from the value label.","principles":"Explore an estate-wide composition with a strong main residence, private suites, connected living and sheltered entertaining. Compose a bespoke arrival, sophisticated roof relationships, deep facades and balanced materials. Pursue carefully resolved craftsmanship and spatial complexity only where useful. Guest facilities, a pool pavilion or wellness rooms may serve the brief without becoming an amenity checklist. These are flexible inspirations, not requirements or price-derived promises.","capabilities":"Translate selected ideas into actual supported scene operations, with coordinated floors, enclosures, openings, entrances, roofs and terraces. Craftsmanship and spatial quality remain design intentions until supported by geometry and review. Disclose missing access, interiors and other unsupported capabilities; a price label does not prove quality.","construction":{"supports":"Coordinate supporting enclosure and roof/floor datums atomically; entrances and terraces need actual connections and access.","materials":"Select available materials and facade depth for local character and maintainability; conceptual finishes do not prove craftsmanship.","operations":["add","replace","move","resize","finish"],"unsupported":"No valuation, construction-cost estimate, automatic programme, engineering, services, code or luxury certification.","requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"]}}
{"id":"facade-materials","version":1,"category":"materials","when":"A residence needing coherent enclosure and material expression.","title":"Facade depth, roofs and material identity","combinations":"Coordinate a small material palette, roof edges, recessed entrances and shaded openings.","placement":"Relate facade rhythm to rooms and privacy; carry architectural intent around side and rear elevations.","principles":"Adapt material and roof recommendations to climate and style instead of prescribing a fixed house template.","capabilities":"Existing ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage; flat, gable and hip roofs; curved roof only via approved open pavilion.","construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["wall"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"Existing ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage; flat, gable and hip roofs; curved roof only via approved open pavilion. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"roof-main-secondary","version":1,"category":"roof-outdoor","when":"Use when the brief or chosen programme calls for primary and secondary roof hierarchy.","title":"Primary and secondary roof hierarchy","combinations":"Timber deck and ivory or limestone roof edges; guards may use the balcony glass primitive.","placement":"Give the principal occupied volume a clear roof and set lower roofs over subordinate spaces.","principles":"Do not let lower roofs intersect upper room windows.","capabilities":"Use direct-scene primitives: plate, roof. No automatic stairs, waterproofing, drainage, roof loading or guard compliance certification.","construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","roof"],"materials":"Timber deck and ivory or limestone roof edges; guards may use the balcony glass primitive.","supports":"Support elevated decks with walls or posts, guard exposed edges, provide actual door access and supported shade.","unsupported":"No automatic stairs, waterproofing, drainage, roof loading or guard compliance certification."}}
